10. COMPLIANCE, SAFETY AND LANGUAGE
- The SEBI-style standards: all the documents carry the registration number, the exchange memberships and the DP details placeholders; the contract notes and the statements follow the regulatory field list; the support and the grievance screens show the escalation matrix and the SCORES link; the referral and the promotional text use the Phase 7 banned-words lint (extend the list: "earn money fast", "free money", "limited time", "guaranteed").
- No dark patterns in the account closure, the consent withdrawal or the notification opt-out: these flows are as easy as the sign-up ones, with neutral wording and no retention nags beyond one neutral confirmation.
- The sensitive data handling: the PII is masked by default in the UI and the logs, the screenshots are blocked on the Profile, the Reports and the Support attachments (FLAG_SECURE, the Phase 1 pattern), the PDFs are password-protected, the signed URLs expire, the downloads are logged, and the chat and ticket attachments are virus-scanned through a scanner provider interface (a mock by default).
- A "Mock data" label on every simulated provider response (the DP statement, the e-sign and the signed contract note).

