RULES
- Keep the UI uncluttered: the Profile tab is a clean list, the reports and the support flows show the common actions first, and the advanced options sit behind clear controls.
- Label all mock data and the simulated signatures. No real email, SMS, document signature or deletion of the real data may ever be triggered in mock mode.
- Money is stored as integer paise or BigDecimal, never as floating point, and every figure in a report must be traceable to the ledger and the trade records.
- No advice, hype, pressure or dark patterns. Follow SEBI and DPDP Act investor-protection and data-protection norms.
- Write production-quality, documented code. No placeholders in logic, only in third-party credentials and the clearly marked Phase 10 hooks (the hardening, the full test suite, the compliance sign-off and the release).